Rules:
  [L1] Use structured logging (JSON format).
  [L2] Include request ID in all logs.
  [L3] Use log levels (DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR).
  [L4] Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens).
  [L5] Use correlation IDs across services.
  [L6] Log at appropriate levels.
  [L7] Use centralized logging (ELK, Loki).
  [L8] Implement log rotation and retention.

Pros:
  - Debugging
  - Audit trail
  - Monitoring

Cons:
  - Storage cost
  - Noise
  - Performance impact

Alternatives:
  - Metrics only
  - Tracing only

